# Build output.
/target/

# The release archives packaging/release.* stages. They are built from a tag,
# uploaded to the GitHub release, and downloaded by every installer; nothing
# here is source and none of it is reproducible from the repository alone
# without the toolchain that built it.
/dist/

# The corpus and its vectors. Both are large and both are rebuilt from public
# sources by scripts/fetch-public-corpus.sh, so neither belongs in the repository.
# Keeping the text out also means the share alike licences of the Wikipedia
# material are satisfied by attribution rather than by redistribution.
*.cache
*.vectors
corpus.jsonl
/index.inillucent/

# The RAG example's chunks, which `scripts/chunk-corpus.py` splits out of the
# corpus beside them in a second. The articles are source and are committed; a
# second copy of the same text, cut into passages, is not.
/examples/rag-agent/corpus/chunks.csv
/examples/rag-agent/corpus/chunks-fts.csv

# Engine databases and their log segments, wherever a test or a scratch run
# leaves one. These are output, never source: no `.rdb` has ever been tracked,
# and `drivers/inillucent-driver/other.rdb` is what an uncommitted directory
# looks like once somebody has run its tests in place.
*.rdb
*.rdb-wal.*
*.rdb-journal

# With one exception, and it is the point of the thing it belongs to.
# `examples/rag-agent/greek-philosophy.rdb` is the example's deliverable: a
# corpus that is already embedded, so a reader asks a question in their first
# minute instead of spending an afternoon building one. A database that has to
# be built before it can be searched is exactly what that example exists to
# remove, so this one is source. `scripts/build-database.sh` rebuilds it, and
# the log segment beside it is still output.
!/examples/rag-agent/greek-philosophy.rdb

# The same for `.db`, but only inside a crate, because `.db` is also SQLite's
# own extension and `compat/fixtures/` holds a hundred tracked files that are
# genuinely source - the files a reader is meant to open with SQLite to check a
# claim. A test that opens a database on the real file system by a relative
# name leaves it in whichever crate directory `cargo test` ran from, and the
# ones seen so far are `app.db`, its log segments, and the scratch file a
# `VACUUM` leaves beside them.
/crates/*/*.db
/crates/*/*.db-wal.*
/crates/*/*.db-journal
/crates/*/*.db.vacuum-*

# Editor and operating system noise.
.DS_Store
/.quill/
/runs/

# The pinned SQLite reference build. Downloaded and verified by
# tools/sqlite-reference.*, used only as a test oracle, never shipped.
/.sqlite-ref/

# Agent-produced artifacts: measurements, scratch renders, harness output. The
# evidence that gates a release is not here - it is checked in under compat/,
# because the compatibility report is generated from it.
/_agent_output/

# The scorecard's working databases, when a run is pointed at the release
# directory. The reports belong in the repository; the pristine images it
# clones per round are hundreds of megabytes and are rebuilt by any run.
/compat/release/small/
/compat/release/medium/
/compat/release/large/

# cargo-mutants writes its run directory here when --output is not given.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# Retired tests, kept rather than deleted (task-1838 §9, Jason's ruling).
#
# The sixteen tests that asserted SQLite *file-format* interoperability - a
# requirement task-1816 dropped when the new engine stopped writing SQLite files
# - are moved here instead of being removed, so the history of what was once
# promised is still on disk and readable. Nothing here is compiled: cargo only
# looks in `tests/`.
/_junk/

# The reference Python binding is run from its own directory, and CPython
# writes its bytecode cache beside it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The npm packages packages/npm/build.mjs assembles from dist/. The manifests
# and the shims are source; the staged tree is a copy of them with the built
# binaries beside it, and it is rebuilt from dist/ every release.
/packages/npm/staged/
*.tgz

# The Python wheel packages/python/build.py assembles, and everything it stages
# into the package to do it. The manifests, the shims and the __init__ are
# source; the binaries, the C ABI library, the header, the licence copy and
# `driver.py` are all copied in from elsewhere in the repository at build time,
# and a second tracked copy of any of them is a copy that would go stale.
/packages/python/build/
/packages/python/dist/
/packages/python/LICENSE
**/*.egg-info/
/packages/python/src/inillucent/_bin/
/packages/python/src/inillucent/_lib/
/packages/python/src/inillucent/_include/
/packages/python/src/inillucent/driver.py

# Composer's own output, and the binaries packages/php/bin/inillucent-install
# downloads into the package at run time.
/vendor/
/composer.lock
/packages/php/runtime/

# The Unluminous IDE's per-workspace state: which files are open, which folders
# are expanded. It belongs to whoever has the checkout open, not to the
# checkout. `tests/selection.toml` has a rule for it too, so a change to it
# selects nothing rather than every suite in the workspace.
/.unluminous/

# The release toolchain tools/cross/fetch-toolchain.ps1 downloads: zig,
# cargo-zigbuild, rcodesign, nfpm and minisign. Somebody else's binaries, pinned
# by SHA-256 in that script and re-fetchable in a minute, so the pin is the
# source and these are not.
/tools/cross/bin/
/tools/cross/cache/
